data.content:
Program runs successfully. Here's what it demonstrates:

---

**1. Strongly-typed retrieval** — use `options.GetTypeInfo(typeof(T))` and cast to `JsonTypeInfo<T>`:

```csharp
JsonTypeInfo<Person> personInfo = (JsonTypeInfo<Person>)options.GetTypeInfo(typeof(Person));
```

> In .NET 9+ there's no built-in generic `GetTypeInfo<T>()` on `JsonSerializerOptions` itself, so the cast is needed. If you want a one-liner helper you can write an extension method.

**2. Probe without throwing** — `TryGetTypeInfo` returns `bool`:

```csharp
if (options.TryGetTypeInfo(typeof(Person), out JsonTypeInfo? info))
{
    // metadata available — cast to JsonTypeInfo<Person> if needed
}
else
{
    // not available, no exception
}
```

When the resolver is `null` (or simply doesn't know the type), `TryGetTypeInfo` returns `false` instead of throwing.
